WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:56.013
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.310
EUN-SU, HUI-SU AND US

3
00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.029
Mr. Jin!

4
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.573
Hui-su has disappeared.

5
00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:15.074
What do you mean?

6
00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.159
What if Jang Kang got her?

7
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.578
Or Jin-young could have
done something to her!

8
00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.830
Cool it. Just pull yourself together.

9
00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:23.249
We're gonna find her, okay?

10
00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:27.003
- You need to find Jang Kang.
- Yes, sir.

11
00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:36.512
Some woman called
Hui-su's mother's nursing home,

12
00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:38.139
claiming she was her niece.

13
00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:39.641
It's Jin-young.

14
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.351
- Eun-su.
- Yeah?

15
00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:43.561
We've got this.

16
00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:04.164
MOM
I'M SORRY TO LEAVE YOU ALL ALONE

17
00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:06.625
I COMMITTED AN UNFORGIVABLE SIN
I KILLED JIN-PYO

18
00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.544
EUN-SU

19
00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:18.345
People always take the elevator,
even if it's just one floor.

20
00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:21.181
When people go to the garage,
they don't even think of using the stairs

21
00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:22.558
'cause they have stuff to carry.

22
00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:25.144
{\an8}That's why the camera in the stairwell
wasn't repaired right away.

23
00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.646
{\an8}Nothing ever happens there.

24
00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:29.356
It sucks we don't have any footage.

25
00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:33.485
I mean, I get it. In apartment complexes,
new expenses need residential approval,

26
00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.195
and there's lots of red tape and stuff.

27
00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:38.116
{\an8}People never take action
until someone gets hurt.

28
00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:39.951
{\an8}Hey, you see that?

29
00:02:40.451 --> 00:02:41.536
<i>I'm thinking</i>

30
00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:45.122
<i>the bastard knows
how to avoid surveillance cameras.</i>

31
00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.792
Or the bitch.

32
00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.544
What?

33
00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.966
Why would she... try to mislead us?

34
00:03:00.471 --> 00:03:01.347
Gyeong-gu?

35
00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:02.807
What's up?

36
00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:10.063
SEARCHING
BREEZE H...

37
00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:15.862
POLICE ACADEMY
SEARCH ALUMNI

38
00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:20.283
NOH JIN-YOUNG
12 PYEONGCHANG 7-GIL

39
00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:31.376
GANGNAM POLICE STATION

40
00:03:51.439 --> 00:03:52.732
What's the matter? It's late.

41
00:03:53.441 --> 00:03:55.485
Yeah, I know, Jin-young. So sorry.

42
00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:57.903
I wouldn't have called you,
but here's the thing.

43
00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.988
You know the surveillance footage
for the murder case

44
00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:01.949
<i>at your brother's apartment complex?</i>

45
00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.034
Mm.

46
00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:07.038
Some of it was corrupted,
but we were able to restore it.

47
00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:09.582
You were?

48
00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:13.543
Yeah, and I saw your brother.
He was in a part that was erased.

49
00:04:13.544 --> 00:04:14.754
It was so weird.

50
00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.179
My brother?

51
00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:25.974
That's not possible.

52
00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:29.184
Listen, did you see it?

53
00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:31.771
Were you able to see the part
where your brother appeared?

54
00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.985
You're making it sound like
I'm the one who deleted it.

55
00:04:41.739 --> 00:04:45.075
He's family. It's only normal
to wanna protect your loved ones.

56
00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:46.703
I didn't protect anyone.

57
00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:50.081
I never saw my brother on the footage.
It couldn't have been him anyway.

58
00:04:52.709 --> 00:04:55.920
Yeah, well, I was told
your brother was there that day, actually.

59
00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.092
My sister-in-law said so, right?

60
00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:03.302
Ah, well, I'm not at liberty to say.

61
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.179
<i>Did you check my brother's travel records?</i>

62
00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:07.056
Did you look into it?

63
00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:13.187
He wasn't even in the country.

64
00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.816
I remember telling you that.

65
00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.277
My sister-in-law's a loose cannon.

66
00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.653
She once hurt herself
to make it seem like--

67
00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:25.867
No, I verified her medical records.
It was clearly a case of domestic abuse.

68
00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:28.911
What?

69
00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:32.247
What's this about?

70
00:05:32.248 --> 00:05:34.541
It's beside the point.
Look, I gotta get going.

71
00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:36.210
Hey, did you speak to my sister-in-law?

72
00:05:37.086 --> 00:05:38.838
I gotta go. Talk later.

73
00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.050
Gimme a sec.

74
00:05:46.971 --> 00:05:48.056
Shit.

75
00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:54.978
MOM

76
00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:57.856
Hi.

77
00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.984
Sweetheart, I'm very confused.
The police are here. It's still dark out.

78
00:06:00.985 --> 00:06:03.779
<i>They keep ringing the doorbell,
asking for Jin-pyo.</i>

79
00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.323
Don't let them in!

80
00:06:06.074 --> 00:06:07.909
Ask to see their badges! Get their names!

81
00:06:08.493 --> 00:06:11.287
They have to tell you
what station they're from, okay?

82
00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:15.499
Right. It's Detective Choi Gyeong-gu.

83
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.460
- From the Gangnam Police Station.
- Oh no!

84
00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.211
Don't let him in!

85
00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:22.089
- He says it'll only take five minutes.
- Oh God! Don't say a word!

86
00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.342
Don't answer the door,
and don't pick up the phone.

87
00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:28.179
And when the cops leave,
head over to my place.

88
00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.722
Why should I do that?

89
00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.183
Too many people
know where you live is all.

90
00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:36.228
Just listen to me
and do what I'm saying, Mom!

91
00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.979
<i>I'll head over there now.</i>

92
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.190
Wait, Jin-young.

93
00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:52.995
Gyeong-gu.

94
00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:54.579
Yeah, what's up?

95
00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.332
Turns out, Mr. Noh was out of the country.

96
00:06:57.333 --> 00:06:58.250
What?

97
00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:00.628
He left the country
a month and a half ago.

98
00:07:05.883 --> 00:07:08.428
JO HUI-SU

99
00:07:21.357 --> 00:07:23.483
DETECTIVE CHOI HERE
FROM THE GANGNAM STATION

100
00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:29.573
<i>You must be swamped,
but you take time to come check in.</i>

101
00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:32.284
You really are one of a kind.
You know the saying,

102
00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:34.412
"Connections aren't beside you,
but above you?"

103
00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:39.499
Do you think you can provide me
with connections from now on?

104
00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.502
I'll do my very best to help.

105
00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:46.006
I'll make sure to give your best regards
to Chief Min.

106
00:07:46.007 --> 00:07:47.550
Great!

107
00:07:49.051 --> 00:07:51.970
Sir, uh, have you heard about the guard

108
00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:54.264
that was killed
at the Breeze Apartment Complex?

109
00:07:54.265 --> 00:07:56.017
It's actually in your jurisdiction.

110
00:07:56.517 --> 00:07:57.643
I have.

111
00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.687
Chief Min's on the case.

112
00:08:00.938 --> 00:08:01.772
And?

113
00:08:03.024 --> 00:08:06.485
This woman told me about her mother,
who lives alone in the complex.

114
00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:08.905
She seems legitimately worried.

115
00:08:09.405 --> 00:08:12.532
She said the young detective in charge
had been poking around a lot.

116
00:08:12.533 --> 00:08:14.701
It's making the residents
feel uncomfortable.

117
00:08:14.702 --> 00:08:16.453
Really?

118
00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:19.790
Yes, she even asked if we could
take him off the investigation.

119
00:08:26.422 --> 00:08:27.672
- Jin-young.
- Hey!

120
00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.382
- Congratulations, Jin-young.
- Well done.

121
00:08:29.383 --> 00:08:31.427
- Congrats, Jin-young!
- Great going!

122
00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:38.266
<i>♪ You're the best one for the job ♪</i>

123
00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:41.353
<i>♪ You're the best one for the job ♪</i>

124
00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:45.065
<i>♪ You're the best one
You're the best one ♪</i>

125
00:08:45.066 --> 00:08:48.026
<i>♪ You're the best one for the job ♪</i>

126
00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:21.435
No!

127
00:09:36.701 --> 00:09:38.119
<i>Hui-su's alive.</i>

128
00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.889
That was Jin-young.

129
00:10:07.398 --> 00:10:08.274
Hui-su!

130
00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.067
Hang on!

131
00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.404
Hui-su!

132
00:10:14.405 --> 00:10:17.073
Hui-su! Wake up, Hui-su!

133
00:10:17.074 --> 00:10:18.241
- It's all right.
- Hui-su!

134
00:10:18.242 --> 00:10:20.328
- No, Hui-su--
- Let's get her to a hospital.

135
00:10:20.911 --> 00:10:22.163
Oh my God!

136
00:10:23.873 --> 00:10:25.040
This is bad.

137
00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:33.466
Move, dammit!

138
00:10:34.508 --> 00:10:36.676
Excuse me, ma'am! Hey, wait!

139
00:10:36.677 --> 00:10:38.011
EMERGENCY ROOM

140
00:10:38.012 --> 00:10:40.889
Ms. Jo Hui-su
was just transferred to Seoul.

141
00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.974
Which hospital? Where was she taken?

142
00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:45.353
I can't share that information with you.

143
00:10:50.024 --> 00:10:51.817
I need it for an investigation.

144
00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:54.070
Uh, one moment, please.

145
00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:00.700
HUI-SU

146
00:11:01.786 --> 00:11:03.870
<i>The caller you are trying to reach
is not available.</i>

147
00:11:03.871 --> 00:11:05.080
<i>Please leave a message.</i>

148
00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.547
Where are you?

149
00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:18.301
Where is she?

150
00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:26.852
You're evil.

151
00:11:28.312 --> 00:11:29.896
I'm not the one who has committed murder.

152
00:11:29.897 --> 00:11:32.315
You knew what he was doing to her.

153
00:11:32.316 --> 00:11:33.608
If you'd tried to help her,

154
00:11:33.609 --> 00:11:35.820
justice could've been served,
and he'd be alive.

155
00:11:36.862 --> 00:11:39.365
You're a psychopath.

156
00:11:40.616 --> 00:11:42.701
You killed him, and you wanna blame me?

157
00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:45.078
All right! Go tell the cops!

158
00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.665
You've got no proof of anything,
you idiot.

159
00:11:48.874 --> 00:11:51.710
- You know what he did.
- What about what you bitches did?

160
00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:55.965
Hui-su should've died last night.

161
00:11:56.882 --> 00:11:59.093
Then maybe I'd have let you live.

162
00:12:00.511 --> 00:12:01.929
Did you tell her

163
00:12:03.097 --> 00:12:05.641
to kill herself in order to keep me alive?

164
00:12:07.685 --> 00:12:09.394
Unbelievable.

165
00:12:10.604 --> 00:12:12.523
I wasn't thinking.

166
00:12:14.567 --> 00:12:17.695
You should've died together
in a suicide pact.

167
00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:21.197
Listen closely, you monster.

168
00:12:21.198 --> 00:12:24.909
If you mess with Hui-su again,
I'll destroy your precious little career.

169
00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.286
So back the fuck off.

170
00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:32.626
Yeah?

171
00:12:33.335 --> 00:12:35.463
If I backed off, you bitch,

172
00:12:36.464 --> 00:12:38.591
I'd have never come this far.

173
00:12:40.217 --> 00:12:41.886
You won't win.

174
00:12:43.512 --> 00:12:45.306
I'll make sure you pay.

175
00:12:56.776 --> 00:12:58.276
{\an8}CHAIRMAN JANG MIN-HO FROM WANGSIMNI

176
00:12:58.277 --> 00:13:00.236
{\an8}MRS. YANG JU-SEON FROM APGUJEONG-DONG

177
00:13:00.237 --> 00:13:03.199
{\an8}WIFE OF 5-TERM ASSEMBLYMAN
HWANG JUN-MO

178
00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:11.457
I think she'll make a full recovery, sir.

179
00:14:02.424 --> 00:14:04.009
{\an8}JIN-YOUNG
5 MISSED CALLS

180
00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.016
RECENTS
JIN-YOUNG

181
00:14:18.065 --> 00:14:19.816
<i>This is Detective Choi Gyeong-gu.</i>

182
00:14:19.817 --> 00:14:22.986
<i>I fear you may not have been
completely honest with me yesterday.</i>

183
00:14:22.987 --> 00:14:24.946
<i>Please contact me immediately.</i>

184
00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:29.451
JIN-YOUNG
ATTACHMENT: 1 VIDEO

185
00:14:31.662 --> 00:14:34.373
<i>Another person has to die
because of you.</i>

186
00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:36.041
<i>Too bad.</i>

187
00:14:37.042 --> 00:14:38.501
<i>Hui-su! Wake up!</i>

188
00:14:38.502 --> 00:14:40.296
<i>Eun-su, can you get the door?</i>

189
00:14:57.938 --> 00:14:58.939
Hey!

190
00:15:00.107 --> 00:15:01.442
Are you okay?

191
00:15:03.861 --> 00:15:05.029
I am, yeah.

192
00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.407
I know you can't eat yet,

193
00:15:08.991 --> 00:15:10.743
so just look at it for now.

194
00:15:11.535 --> 00:15:14.412
They say red is supposed to
make your mouth water, boost energy,

195
00:15:14.413 --> 00:15:16.081
and give you courage.

196
00:15:21.337 --> 00:15:23.172
You talked with Jin-young, right?

197
00:15:29.178 --> 00:15:30.220
You know what?

198
00:15:33.724 --> 00:15:35.976
I've gotta say these past few weeks

199
00:15:36.894 --> 00:15:38.771
made me feel so alive.

200
00:15:46.737 --> 00:15:48.905
I've been letting my guard down.

201
00:15:48.906 --> 00:15:50.573
I feel safe.

202
00:15:50.574 --> 00:15:51.867
I'm at peace.

203
00:15:54.995 --> 00:15:56.747
That, to me, is a huge win.

204
00:16:07.091 --> 00:16:09.426
I feel like over the past few months...

205
00:16:11.804 --> 00:16:14.932
I've gotten a little closer
to stepping out of the darkness.

206
00:16:27.861 --> 00:16:30.239
All right. Enough waiting. I'm starving.

207
00:16:48.173 --> 00:16:49.174
Ms. Jo.

208
00:16:50.217 --> 00:16:52.136
- Oh.
- You're off today, aren't you?

209
00:16:53.303 --> 00:16:56.222
You're right, but I had the feeling
someone would come to see me.

210
00:16:56.223 --> 00:16:57.391
Oh.

211
00:16:58.475 --> 00:16:59.518
You're doing great.

212
00:17:01.186 --> 00:17:02.563
Are you Jo Eun-su?

213
00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.315
Yes.

214
00:17:06.275 --> 00:17:07.900
I need you to come with us
for questioning.

215
00:17:07.901 --> 00:17:11.070
- On suspicion of accepting a bribe.
- Let's go to the station, ma'am.

216
00:17:26.628 --> 00:17:28.213
JO EUN-SU

217
00:17:44.605 --> 00:17:46.606
RECORDING

218
00:17:56.742 --> 00:17:58.452
STANDBY

219
00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:10.339
Any thoughts
now that you're here?

220
00:18:16.345 --> 00:18:18.347
Is Jang Kang better hidden this time?

221
00:18:21.183 --> 00:18:23.685
I gave it some thought
and figured it was you.

222
00:18:25.187 --> 00:18:26.605
Is he still alive and well?

223
00:18:29.066 --> 00:18:31.235
There's no need for you
to worry about that.

224
00:18:34.988 --> 00:18:37.241
We need to finish our talk from earlier.

225
00:18:41.203 --> 00:18:44.248
I hear your father is about to retire.

226
00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:49.710
I know he was
just a low-level civil servant,

227
00:18:49.711 --> 00:18:51.672
but he still deserves to get

228
00:18:53.006 --> 00:18:55.884
one of those plaques
with his name engraved on it.

229
00:18:58.178 --> 00:18:59.888
Don't you think he should get one?

230
00:19:05.811 --> 00:19:08.397
How long do you think
your mother will take to get here?

231
00:19:12.025 --> 00:19:13.610
I want Hui-su.

232
00:19:29.626 --> 00:19:30.501
Yes, ma'am?

233
00:19:30.502 --> 00:19:33.671
Is it true that you assisted
your older brother in fleeing the country?

234
00:19:33.672 --> 00:19:35.673
He's a white-collar criminal
and embezzler?

235
00:19:35.674 --> 00:19:36.591
Excuse me?

236
00:19:36.592 --> 00:19:39.468
<i>And did you put pressure
on his securities firm to cover it up?</i>

237
00:19:42.389 --> 00:19:43.891
Of course not.

238
00:19:44.391 --> 00:19:45.892
I'd never do that, ma'am.

239
00:19:45.893 --> 00:19:49.479
<i>I expect a formal response in my office
by the end of the day.</i>

240
00:19:50.063 --> 00:19:51.063
Ma'am?

241
00:19:55.068 --> 00:19:56.445
Shit.

242
00:20:15.714 --> 00:20:19.593
I didn't mention how violent he was,
and what followed.

243
00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:24.556
Stop fucking with me!

244
00:20:25.057 --> 00:20:26.225
Hey, easy!

245
00:20:26.725 --> 00:20:29.853
- Ms. Jo's attorney's here!
- How dare you assault my client!

246
00:20:34.566 --> 00:20:36.817
Fuck me.

247
00:20:46.495 --> 00:20:48.121
Please, wait here a moment.

248
00:20:56.213 --> 00:20:58.215
Mr. Jin sent me, ma'am.

249
00:21:28.829 --> 00:21:30.247
MOM

250
00:21:30.831 --> 00:21:32.206
I'm driving. I'll call you later!

251
00:21:32.207 --> 00:21:34.251
<i>Jin-young! It's that man.</i>

252
00:21:34.751 --> 00:21:37.296
- I can't hear you. I'll call you later!
<i>- Jin-young!</i>

253
00:21:38.213 --> 00:21:41.049
<i>It's that... that man.</i>

254
00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:06.116
Thank you, Mr. Jin.

255
00:22:06.616 --> 00:22:10.619
Go get both your passports and suitcases.

256
00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:13.956
Once I get the two of you on a flight,
I'll handle the rest.

257
00:22:13.957 --> 00:22:16.043
- Not a chance!
- Cut it out.

258
00:23:06.718 --> 00:23:07.552
Uh-huh?

259
00:23:11.431 --> 00:23:13.850
Jang Kang could be there, so stay alert.

260
00:23:27.531 --> 00:23:28.447
Please...

261
00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:34.287
Shit.

262
00:23:41.711 --> 00:23:43.380
Oh shit.

263
00:24:06.194 --> 00:24:08.947
A FEW HOURS AGO

264
00:24:44.483 --> 00:24:46.359
J... Jin-pyo?

265
00:24:50.780 --> 00:24:52.616
Jin-pyo! Jin-pyo!

266
00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:56.328
What are you doing on the floor?
Come on. Get up, Jin-pyo!

267
00:24:56.912 --> 00:24:59.372
Wake up! Jin-pyo! Oh!

268
00:25:00.081 --> 00:25:01.832
What's going on with you? Goodness!

269
00:25:01.833 --> 00:25:02.959
Mom.

270
00:25:04.169 --> 00:25:05.962
Could you untie me?

271
00:25:13.887 --> 00:25:14.887
Who are you?

272
00:25:14.888 --> 00:25:16.973
I'm Jin-pyo.

273
00:25:17.474 --> 00:25:18.391
Your son.

274
00:25:19.142 --> 00:25:19.976
Mom?

275
00:25:20.477 --> 00:25:22.186
Mom, I'm in pain.

276
00:25:22.187 --> 00:25:23.687
Please untie me.

277
00:25:23.688 --> 00:25:25.523
Th... That watch.

278
00:25:25.524 --> 00:25:27.150
It's Jin-pyo's.

279
00:25:27.734 --> 00:25:30.277
Give it back!
Why the hell are you wearing it?

280
00:25:30.278 --> 00:25:32.906
For fuck's sake.
Who cares about the watch?

281
00:25:33.657 --> 00:25:34.741
- Shit!
- Ah!

282
00:25:35.659 --> 00:25:37.451
Like mother, like daughter.

283
00:25:37.452 --> 00:25:39.579
Wow, you two are really alike.

284
00:25:41.122 --> 00:25:43.959
You probably don't care Jin-pyo's dead.

285
00:25:47.420 --> 00:25:48.255
What?

286
00:25:49.548 --> 00:25:50.382
He's...

287
00:25:51.258 --> 00:25:52.717
What did you just say?

288
00:25:55.220 --> 00:25:58.265
Your son is dead. Gone forever.

289
00:25:59.182 --> 00:26:00.015
Oh.

290
00:26:00.016 --> 00:26:01.977
It's been a while now.

291
00:26:02.477 --> 00:26:03.811
You're lying!

292
00:26:03.812 --> 00:26:06.730
You should ask your damn daughter
if I'm lying to you.

293
00:26:06.731 --> 00:26:10.569
She knows.
But first, get me the fuck out now!

294
00:26:11.611 --> 00:26:14.863
Tell me what you did to my son.
What did you do?

295
00:26:16.825 --> 00:26:20.620
You really should've raised
your kids better.

296
00:26:23.039 --> 00:26:27.710
You failed.
Your son's a loser. A worthless disgrace.

297
00:26:27.711 --> 00:26:29.962
Fucking hell.

298
00:26:29.963 --> 00:26:33.549
He's the reason my life's
all fucked up right now.

299
00:26:33.550 --> 00:26:35.467
Your precious son's an asshole.

300
00:26:35.468 --> 00:26:37.761
Jin-pyo was just a waste of flesh.

301
00:26:37.762 --> 00:26:39.431
He deserved to die.

302
00:27:08.168 --> 00:27:10.544
This is crazy.

303
00:27:10.545 --> 00:27:13.797
That bastard murdered my baby boy,
didn't he? Didn't he?

304
00:27:13.798 --> 00:27:16.009
- Jin-pyo was killed! What happened?
- Hey!

305
00:27:16.593 --> 00:27:18.970
Do you want us both
to end up like Jin-pyo?

306
00:27:19.888 --> 00:27:23.057
I... could lose everything because of this.

307
00:27:23.058 --> 00:27:25.726
We'll be charged with murder!
You want that?

308
00:27:25.727 --> 00:27:27.687
You need to get a grip, Mom!

309
00:27:28.605 --> 00:27:31.315
Pull yourself together,
or we're both going down.

310
00:27:32.859 --> 00:27:34.193
Keep pushing.

311
00:27:39.908 --> 00:27:40.867
Wait, stop.

312
00:27:41.368 --> 00:27:42.785
Okay, now come. This way.

313
00:27:42.786 --> 00:27:44.244
Lift.

314
00:28:07.936 --> 00:28:08.769
Yeah, what's up?

315
00:28:08.770 --> 00:28:11.271
<i>Jin-young loaded something
into her trunk and left.</i>

316
00:28:11.272 --> 00:28:13.107
<i>I'm pretty sure it's Jang Kang.</i>

317
00:28:13.108 --> 00:28:14.858
<i>I think he's dead, sir.</i>

318
00:28:14.859 --> 00:28:15.860
What?

319
00:28:18.488 --> 00:28:20.072
She's with her mom.

320
00:28:20.073 --> 00:28:22.409
They could be going somewhere
to dump the body.

321
00:28:28.164 --> 00:28:29.206
All right.

322
00:28:29.207 --> 00:28:31.918
On my way now. Just keep a close watch.

323
00:28:32.419 --> 00:28:33.544
Hang on for a sec.

324
00:28:33.545 --> 00:28:34.545
I should go.

325
00:28:34.546 --> 00:28:36.630
That's not an option. Hui-su and--

326
00:28:36.631 --> 00:28:38.133
Please, I have to do it.

327
00:28:40.343 --> 00:28:41.344
No way.

328
00:28:42.929 --> 00:28:45.514
I started this,
so I should be the one to finish it.

329
00:28:45.515 --> 00:28:46.724
Eun-su, it'll be over soon.

330
00:28:46.725 --> 00:28:49.685
It's almost over. I just need you
to take Hui-su and leave the country.

331
00:28:49.686 --> 00:28:51.437
- Could you please do that?
- Mr. Jin.

332
00:28:51.438 --> 00:28:52.814
Yes, what do you want?

333
00:29:20.550 --> 00:29:21.384
Ma.

334
00:29:23.136 --> 00:29:24.804
Are you sure Jang Kang's dead?

335
00:29:27.849 --> 00:29:29.184
Okay, I gotta get going.

336
00:29:33.730 --> 00:29:35.273
Please take care of Hui-su.

337
00:29:36.441 --> 00:29:37.442
Eun-su?

338
00:29:46.534 --> 00:29:48.620
I want you to have this just in case.

339
00:29:55.335 --> 00:29:56.211
Okay.

340
00:30:21.528 --> 00:30:23.988
<i>You have gone off-road.</i>

341
00:30:25.907 --> 00:30:28.618
Eun-su's the one going.
I want you to keep your eyes on her.

342
00:30:30.411 --> 00:30:32.872
<i>You have gone off-road.</i>

343
00:30:41.422 --> 00:30:43.550
Hey, um, where did Eun-su go?

344
00:30:49.889 --> 00:30:51.683
You have any idea where she went?

345
00:30:55.270 --> 00:30:56.187
Hmm?

346
00:31:38.855 --> 00:31:40.356
All right. I've got eyes on her car.

347
00:32:20.688 --> 00:32:21.898
Oh shit.

348
00:32:26.069 --> 00:32:28.237
All right. Time to let my crazy bitch out.

349
00:32:37.330 --> 00:32:39.457
I admit I killed my husband.

350
00:32:47.799 --> 00:32:49.216
Somebody should get help.

351
00:32:49.217 --> 00:32:51.218
Call an ambulance or something!

352
00:32:53.012 --> 00:32:54.805
That car crashed
into the other one.

353
00:32:54.806 --> 00:32:56.306
Someone's getting out of that one.

354
00:32:59.060 --> 00:33:01.104
Oh my God. What do we do?

355
00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:04.064
Get the camera!
You've gotta get a shot.

356
00:33:04.065 --> 00:33:05.358
Look, there's a body there!

357
00:33:07.527 --> 00:33:09.486
Goddammit!

358
00:33:12.824 --> 00:33:15.117
Oh shit! Shit! Get away from me!

359
00:33:15.118 --> 00:33:16.660
I know that person!

360
00:33:16.661 --> 00:33:19.455
- Call an ambulance!
- It's that famous lecturer!

361
00:33:20.581 --> 00:33:22.708
Ms. Eun-su, are you okay?

362
00:33:22.709 --> 00:33:23.625
Yeah.

363
00:33:27.839 --> 00:33:29.298
No!

364
00:33:55.908 --> 00:33:57.869
<i>On the night of October 30th,</i>

365
00:33:59.287 --> 00:34:01.497
I killed Noh Jin-pyo.

366
00:34:02.415 --> 00:34:03.832
He was my husband.

367
00:34:08.421 --> 00:34:09.630
And yesterday,

368
00:34:11.340 --> 00:34:13.676
his sister, Jin-Young, tried to kill me.

369
00:34:24.395 --> 00:34:26.773
MA HAE-RYONG

370
00:34:28.858 --> 00:34:29.776
Hey.

371
00:34:43.122 --> 00:34:44.623
<i>Around 7:00 p.m. tonight,</i>

372
00:34:44.624 --> 00:34:47.334
<i>a shocking discovery was made
in a three-car collision</i>

373
00:34:47.335 --> 00:34:48.585
<i>near the outskirts of Seoul.</i>

374
00:34:48.586 --> 00:34:53.423
<i>The body of a man was found inside
the trunk of one of the impacted vehicles.</i>

375
00:34:53.424 --> 00:34:56.259
<i>The police have taken three drivers
and one passenger</i>

376
00:34:56.260 --> 00:34:58.512
<i>involved in the crash into custody.</i>

377
00:34:58.513 --> 00:35:00.806
<i>The driver of the vehicle
carrying the body</i>

378
00:35:00.807 --> 00:35:04.142
<i>has been identified
as an active-duty officer, Captain Noh.</i>

379
00:35:04.143 --> 00:35:05.895
<i>Noh's mother, a well-respected lecturer...</i>

380
00:35:07.021 --> 00:35:08.897
Everything was caught
on the dashcam.

381
00:35:08.898 --> 00:35:10.565
There's no way she can deny it.

382
00:35:10.566 --> 00:35:12.025
Why would she do that?

383
00:35:12.026 --> 00:35:13.194
Get to work.

384
00:35:15.071 --> 00:35:16.864
Mind your business. Go on.

385
00:35:19.200 --> 00:35:20.909
If you're feeling overwhelmed,

386
00:35:20.910 --> 00:35:23.412
we can stop for today
and talk some more tomorrow.

387
00:35:24.288 --> 00:35:26.082
No, we don't need to stop.

388
00:35:29.460 --> 00:35:31.462
You and Hui-su are so alike.

389
00:35:35.258 --> 00:35:37.510
I need to know if she's all right.

390
00:35:39.345 --> 00:35:40.304
She is.

391
00:35:44.016 --> 00:35:45.433
That's so good to hear.

392
00:35:45.434 --> 00:35:46.894
I'll tell you everything.

393
00:35:56.195 --> 00:35:57.905
I visited with Ms. Jo.

394
00:35:59.866 --> 00:36:01.993
No need to worry.
She's gonna be all right.

395
00:36:08.958 --> 00:36:10.209
Thanks so much, sir.

396
00:36:55.296 --> 00:36:58.132
We will present
the best possible defense.

397
00:37:04.222 --> 00:37:05.889
LAW FIRM BAEKSAN

398
00:37:05.890 --> 00:37:08.392
Of course you will.
You're costing me a fortune.

399
00:37:13.606 --> 00:37:15.357
<i>Another murder
and attempted murder</i>

400
00:37:15.358 --> 00:37:17.859
<i>came to light
during further investigation.</i>

401
00:37:17.860 --> 00:37:21.655
<i>The police now suspect the incident
was not merely a traffic accident,</i>

402
00:37:21.656 --> 00:37:24.658
<i>but may be connected
to a far more serious crime.</i>

403
00:37:24.659 --> 00:37:28.328
<i>New video footage has surfaced
showing Noh, while on active duty,</i>

404
00:37:28.329 --> 00:37:31.248
<i>attempting to murder
her sister-in-law, Jo Hui-su,</i>

405
00:37:31.249 --> 00:37:33.667
<i>and staging her death as a suicide.</i>

406
00:37:33.668 --> 00:37:37.003
<i>Noh remained silent
while being transported to police lockup.</i>

407
00:37:37.004 --> 00:37:39.589
<i>Her alleged involvement
in such criminal activities</i>

408
00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:42.217
<i>has brought significant disgrace
to the police force.</i>

409
00:37:50.810 --> 00:37:52.311
How are you gonna plead?

410
00:38:02.697 --> 00:38:04.699
YOU ARE NO WOMEN'S ADVOCATE!
KO JEONG-SUK OUT

411
00:38:05.783 --> 00:38:06.950
Hey!

412
00:38:06.951 --> 00:38:10.578
Your twisted love for your child
is why he was murdered!

413
00:38:10.579 --> 00:38:11.872
It's your fault!

414
00:38:15.042 --> 00:38:18.211
You. I will sue you for defamation.

415
00:38:18.212 --> 00:38:20.088
My son was the victim!

416
00:38:20.089 --> 00:38:22.841
And I'm a victim too!
You can go straight to hell!

417
00:38:22.842 --> 00:38:25.219
Now it's about to be
where you're going, lady!

418
00:38:25.720 --> 00:38:27.971
<i>The officer's mother,
also accused of the crime,</i>

419
00:38:27.972 --> 00:38:29.931
<i>claimed that she was, in fact,
the real victim.</i>

420
00:38:29.932 --> 00:38:31.891
<i>- The crowd reacted with outrage.</i>

421
00:38:31.892 --> 00:38:33.268
<i>Now for the economy.</i>

422
00:38:33.269 --> 00:38:36.062
<i>With the end of the year approaching,
consumer confidence has weakened,</i>

423
00:38:36.063 --> 00:38:37.355
<i>putting the retail industry on...</i>

424
00:38:37.356 --> 00:38:38.440
Hello?

425
00:38:38.441 --> 00:38:42.778
<i>Hello, Mrs. Kim.
I'm calling from Lavie Department Store.</i>

426
00:38:43.279 --> 00:38:45.864
<i>I want to sincerely apologize
for the trouble</i>

427
00:38:45.865 --> 00:38:48.159
<i>one of our employees has caused you.</i>

428
00:38:49.285 --> 00:38:51.244
Everything has been worked out.

429
00:38:51.245 --> 00:38:53.122
<i>Oh, that's good to hear.</i>

430
00:38:53.748 --> 00:38:56.625
I just hope Ms. Jo
isn't seriously injured.

431
00:38:57.877 --> 00:39:00.588
TO MASTER KIM DAE-CHEOL

432
00:39:40.961 --> 00:39:42.505
COURTROOMS

433
00:40:05.986 --> 00:40:07.988
Please make your final statement.

434
00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:25.631
During my marriage,
my husband's behavior made me...

435
00:40:28.592 --> 00:40:30.302
want to end my own life.

436
00:40:33.139 --> 00:40:35.516
I'd speak to the heavens, to no avail.

437
00:40:37.852 --> 00:40:39.687
The beatings were constant.

438
00:40:40.479 --> 00:40:42.565
I was wasting away in unbearable pain.

439
00:40:45.276 --> 00:40:46.735
I came to realize...

440
00:40:49.363 --> 00:40:51.364
it was never going to stop...

441
00:40:53.576 --> 00:40:55.453
...if I didn't take action.

442
00:41:06.881 --> 00:41:08.424
In the end, I...

443
00:41:09.967 --> 00:41:11.927
I decided to kill my husband.

444
00:41:15.890 --> 00:41:19.643
I'm well aware
that I'm to blame for his death.

445
00:41:20.769 --> 00:41:24.648
I understand that there is no excuse
for committing murder.

446
00:41:27.318 --> 00:41:28.777
And so I believe...

447
00:41:30.863 --> 00:41:33.240
I should be punished for my crime.

448
00:41:35.910 --> 00:41:37.535
Defendant Jo Eun-su.

449
00:41:37.536 --> 00:41:39.371
Your final statement, please.

450
00:41:46.962 --> 00:41:49.757
When I was small,
I would hear my mother getting beaten.

451
00:41:51.217 --> 00:41:53.302
I would take my little brother
by the hand,

452
00:41:53.802 --> 00:41:55.846
and we would go hide in the closet.

453
00:41:57.431 --> 00:41:59.099
Then once it grew quiet,

454
00:42:00.017 --> 00:42:02.561
I'd come out, eat, and watch TV.

455
00:42:03.062 --> 00:42:06.565
I would act like everything was fine
and nothing had even happened.

456
00:42:08.943 --> 00:42:11.654
At the time,
I thought it was because I was afraid.

457
00:42:13.155 --> 00:42:14.907
I understood much later

458
00:42:16.617 --> 00:42:18.159
that I'd become indifferent.

459
00:42:18.160 --> 00:42:19.620
I'd learned to look away.

460
00:42:23.666 --> 00:42:27.461
Even as a child, I knew deep down
that domestic violence was a crime.

461
00:42:28.921 --> 00:42:29.755
But

462
00:42:31.382 --> 00:42:35.051
much later,
I realized I was... also to blame.

463
00:42:35.052 --> 00:42:39.139
By pretending I saw nothing,
I was also committing a crime.

464
00:42:41.976 --> 00:42:45.396
I came to that conclusion
many years later, as an adult.

465
00:42:48.274 --> 00:42:51.860
I now understand that it is not only
the abuser who is guilty.

466
00:42:53.612 --> 00:42:56.573
Because if you turn a blind eye,
you are complicit.

467
00:42:56.574 --> 00:42:59.493
Not helping someone
who's being abused is criminal.

468
00:43:02.079 --> 00:43:03.998
I know my actions have shocked many.

469
00:43:07.585 --> 00:43:08.627
But I know

470
00:43:09.587 --> 00:43:12.047
I did everything in my power
to save my friend.

471
00:43:35.904 --> 00:43:37.323
Hey, Gye-sun.

472
00:43:56.342 --> 00:43:58.344
I'm finally free now.

473
00:43:59.595 --> 00:44:01.347
I left the house with Eun-hyeok.

474
00:44:04.683 --> 00:44:06.644
It's not what you think. Don't worry.

475
00:44:07.478 --> 00:44:10.856
I simply collected my things
and walked out of there.

476
00:44:14.068 --> 00:44:15.653
That was all it took.

477
00:44:17.237 --> 00:44:20.115
But for all those years,
I couldn't bring myself to do it.

478
00:44:24.036 --> 00:44:25.788
I am so sorry

479
00:44:26.288 --> 00:44:29.540
for putting you
in that foster home for a while,

480
00:44:29.541 --> 00:44:30.793
when you were little.

481
00:44:33.337 --> 00:44:35.506
I know you remember everything.

482
00:44:37.883 --> 00:44:40.511
Your brother was just a baby, you know?

483
00:44:41.011 --> 00:44:43.097
I figured you'd be safer there

484
00:44:43.597 --> 00:44:46.558
while I got our affairs ready so I could
leave the house with Eun-hyeok.

485
00:44:47.810 --> 00:44:51.105
But then, he fell really ill,
quite suddenly.

486
00:44:52.314 --> 00:44:55.526
Running away
would have put his life at risk.

487
00:44:58.612 --> 00:45:01.614
But the moment I heard you say
you wanted to come home,

488
00:45:01.615 --> 00:45:03.617
I took you out of that place.

489
00:45:04.118 --> 00:45:06.244
But I can only imagine...

490
00:45:11.166 --> 00:45:15.003
...how scared you were
being left there for ten days.

491
00:45:24.722 --> 00:45:28.684
I was just a kid, and I believed
I needed to stay close to my dad.

492
00:45:29.476 --> 00:45:31.645
I wanted us to all be together.

493
00:45:32.229 --> 00:45:34.732
I wasn't concerned about you.

494
00:45:36.942 --> 00:45:39.862
I didn't know any better,

495
00:45:40.362 --> 00:45:43.031
and my selfishness
caused you to stay with Dad.

496
00:45:43.574 --> 00:45:46.033
You ended up spending your whole life
getting beatings from Dad,

497
00:45:46.034 --> 00:45:47.661
not to break up the family.

498
00:45:48.412 --> 00:45:49.872
I knew everything.

499
00:45:51.665 --> 00:45:54.793
And I was afraid
I would end up just like you.

500
00:45:57.254 --> 00:45:58.422
I was a coward.

501
00:45:58.922 --> 00:46:01.216
I didn't have the courage
to face the truth.

502
00:46:04.011 --> 00:46:07.013
I masked all my fear
with a stupid superiority complex,

503
00:46:07.014 --> 00:46:08.849
thinking I was better than you.

504
00:46:11.643 --> 00:46:13.812
I'm so sorry, Mom.

505
00:46:16.732 --> 00:46:18.192
Oh, honey.

506
00:46:19.443 --> 00:46:20.986
And I know...

507
00:46:22.571 --> 00:46:24.198
...I wasn't grateful enough.

508
00:46:26.658 --> 00:46:27.618
Mom...

509
00:46:29.203 --> 00:46:30.913
...thanks for protecting us.

510
00:46:42.966 --> 00:46:46.094
Mom, these are your favorite wildflowers.

511
00:46:51.308 --> 00:46:52.768
I'm doing well now.

512
00:46:53.560 --> 00:46:55.103
My heart's at peace.

513
00:47:02.152 --> 00:47:03.779
Inmate 2083.

514
00:48:22.441 --> 00:48:24.151
Hui-su! Hui-su!

515
00:48:24.776 --> 00:48:26.194
Eun-su! Hi!

516
00:48:27.237 --> 00:48:28.405
Mm.

517
00:48:40.208 --> 00:48:41.251
Mr. Jin.

518
00:48:41.919 --> 00:48:44.338
Ah, Mr. Jin. Thanks for everything.

519
00:48:47.507 --> 00:48:51.218
It wasn't my idea,
but... she insisted I buy it.

520
00:48:51.219 --> 00:48:52.596
Wanna have a bite?

521
00:48:56.099 --> 00:48:57.100
Mmm!

522
00:48:58.268 --> 00:49:00.312
- Delicious!
- Oh yeah?

523
00:49:01.021 --> 00:49:03.606
All right. Enough of this.
You need real food.

524
00:49:03.607 --> 00:49:04.690
- Let's do it.
- Yeah?

525
00:49:04.691 --> 00:49:06.443
I can't wait.

526
00:49:07.361 --> 00:49:10.364
You two have some pretty hard work
ahead of you.

527
00:49:17.204 --> 00:49:18.413
This is nice.

528
00:49:22.292 --> 00:49:24.836
Mom. Dad. You're finally together.

529
00:49:31.593 --> 00:49:33.136
Take care of each other.

530
00:49:34.888 --> 00:49:36.306
I'll come visit soon.

531
00:50:08.797 --> 00:50:10.507
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

532
00:50:13.760 --> 00:50:15.345
Hui-su, can you check this?

533
00:50:25.063 --> 00:50:27.356
- They only use quality ingredients.
- They do.

534
00:50:27.357 --> 00:50:29.400
- You should order more next time.
- Okay.

535
00:50:29.401 --> 00:50:31.777
- Bye, you two. Thanks.
- Okay. Take care.

536
00:50:31.778 --> 00:50:32.820
Thank you.

537
00:50:32.821 --> 00:50:33.905
Sorry.

538
00:50:38.118 --> 00:50:39.618
Hi. How are you?

539
00:50:39.619 --> 00:50:41.996
- Good, but what took you so long?
- Here.

540
00:50:41.997 --> 00:50:42.913
Sorry.

541
00:50:42.914 --> 00:50:45.499
People kept asking me
for this, but I had nothing to sell.

542
00:50:45.500 --> 00:50:46.792
It's here now.

543
00:50:46.793 --> 00:50:48.919
Right, but did you
fulfill the whole order?

544
00:50:48.920 --> 00:50:49.838
Yeah.

545
00:50:52.799 --> 00:50:54.467
So does this look right?

546
00:50:54.468 --> 00:50:55.968
Yeah. This is perfect.

547
00:50:55.969 --> 00:50:57.304
Hey, babe!

548
00:50:58.096 --> 00:50:59.847
Get over here and check this inventory.

549
00:50:59.848 --> 00:51:01.850
Hold your horses. I'm coming.

550
00:51:02.434 --> 00:51:04.685
It's so hot outside.
You want something to drink?

551
00:51:04.686 --> 00:51:05.937
It'll be my treat.

552
00:51:12.694 --> 00:51:13.528
Here.

553
00:51:14.154 --> 00:51:17.574
All right. Let's get ready
to make a wish, okay?

554
00:51:19.785 --> 00:51:20.951
It's floating.

555
00:51:20.952 --> 00:51:22.079
Oh!

556
00:51:39.221 --> 00:51:40.931
Uh...

557
00:51:42.599 --> 00:51:43.892
Did you make a wish?

558
00:51:49.314 --> 00:51:52.108
Look! There it is. See?
It's floating away.

559
00:51:52.109 --> 00:51:53.360
It's beautiful.

560
00:52:00.951 --> 00:52:07.958
THERE IS ALWAYS LIGHT
AT THE END OF THE TUNNEL

561
00:52:13.630 --> 00:52:16.675
<i>I used to
pay very little attention to the weather.</i>

562
00:52:18.301 --> 00:52:19.386
<i>But now,</i>

563
00:52:20.762 --> 00:52:23.932
<i>it's the first thing I wonder about
when I wake up in the morning.</i>

564
00:52:24.808 --> 00:52:27.102
<i>What kind of sky will greet me today?</i>

565
00:52:31.523 --> 00:52:33.399
- Good morning!
- Good morning.

566
00:52:34.526 --> 00:52:35.652
See you later.

567
00:52:36.153 --> 00:52:37.904
- Have a great day!
- Mm-hmm!

568
00:52:50.208 --> 00:52:54.004
<i>Even if good luck doesn't
wash over my life like crashing waves,</i>

569
00:52:54.629 --> 00:52:58.842
<i>and even if rising tides
try to knock me down and swallow me whole...</i>

570
00:53:01.761 --> 00:53:04.263
<i>I've learned not to back down</i>

571
00:53:04.264 --> 00:53:06.850
<i>and to face each challenge with courage.</i>

572
00:53:09.311 --> 00:53:11.813
<i>Because whatever wave
rolls my way tomorrow...</i>

573
00:53:16.610 --> 00:53:18.486
<i>I just need to ride it.</i>

574
00:53:26.494 --> 00:53:28.496
<i>♪ I used to not care ♪</i>

575
00:53:29.039 --> 00:53:31.166
<i>♪ I never felt scared ♪</i>

576
00:53:31.708 --> 00:53:33.793
<i>♪ I only pretend ♪</i>

577
